NEARS-1808 AC2/AC3 — live evidence, emulator-5562, 2026-08-21

=== AC2: two distinct-suffix UserApp APKs installed on the SAME device ===
$ adb install -r app-suffixed-wta.apk   -> Success
$ adb install -r app-suffixed-wtb.apk   -> Success
$ adb shell pm list packages | grep izzes.nears
package:com.izzes.nears
package:com.izzes.nears.wta
package:com.izzes.nears.wtb
RESULT: both com.izzes.nears.wta and com.izzes.nears.wtb (plus the pre-existing unsuffixed
com.izzes.nears from an unrelated foreign session) coexist simultaneously — 3 distinct
package entries, none replaced the other. AC2 CONFIRMED.

=== AC3: pre-fix contrast — reinstalling the SAME unsuffixed id twice ===
(device freed of the foreign com.izzes.nears + wtb first, to stay above the 800MB disk floor
mid-session; re-confirmed after)

$ adb install -r app-unsuffixed.apk   (simulating "worktree A" run)   -> Success
$ adb shell pm list packages | grep 'izzes.nears$'
package:com.izzes.nears

$ adb install -r app-unsuffixed.apk   (simulating "worktree B" run, SAME id)   -> Success
  (no warning, no differing signal from install #1 — Android's package manager treats this as
   a plain update-in-place)
$ adb shell pm list packages | grep izzes.nears
package:com.izzes.nears
package:com.izzes.nears.wta      <- unaffected, proves suffixed builds do NOT collide
RESULT: two consecutive unsuffixed installs collapse to exactly ONE com.izzes.nears entry —
the second silently replaced the first, both installs reporting identical "Success" with no
distinguishing signal. This is the pre-fix clobber (NEARS-1652 incident shape) reproduced live.
Meanwhile the suffixed com.izzes.nears.wta installed earlier was completely unaffected by
either unsuffixed install — the contrast the ticket's AC3 asks for. AC3 CONFIRMED.
